---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageMasthead from "../../components/PageMasthead.astro";
import EditorialImage from "../../components/EditorialImage.astro";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "@id": "https://racquethabit.com/journal/manifesto#article",
  headline: "A Difficult Habit to Break",
  description: "A court note on repeat players, tennis rituals and the hours around play.",
  image: {
    "@type": "ImageObject",
    url: "https://racquethabit.com/images/editorial/shadow-rally.webp",
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://racquethabit.com/journal/manifesto",
  },
  author: { "@id": "https://racquethabit.com/#organization" },
  publisher: { "@id": "https://racquethabit.com/#organization" },
  datePublished: "2026-07-23",
  dateModified: "2026-07-23",
  inLanguage: "en",
};
const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  itemListElement: [
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Journal", item: "https://racquethabit.com/journal" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "A Difficult Habit to Break", item: "https://racquethabit.com/journal/manifesto" },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="A Difficult Habit to Break | Racquet Habit Journal"
  description="Read Court Note 001 on repeat players, tennis rituals and the considered apparel and court goods behind Racquet Habit."
  image="/images/editorial/shadow-rally.webp"
  imageAlt="The shadows of two tennis players meeting at the net"
  pageType="article"
  schema={[articleSchema, breadcrumbSchema]}
>
  <PageMasthead
    title="A difficult habit to break"
    intro="The court is a rectangle. The habit is not nearly so contained. There is always time for another set—or at least that is the working theory."
    issue="Court note 001 · 4 minute read"
    tone="red"
  >
    <div class="article-byline"><span>By Racquet Habit</span><time datetime="2026-07-23">23 July 2026</time></div>
  </PageMasthead>

  <article class="annual-article">
    <EditorialImage
      src="/images/editorial/shadow-rally.webp"
      alt="The shadows of two tennis players meeting at the net"
      caption="The final set develops sequels"
      plate="Opening plate"
      eager
    />
    <div class="annual-article__body">
      <aside><span>Journal no. 001</span><span>Society file</span><span>Subject: repeat players</span></aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">It starts with one booking. Then another racquet, a preferred grip, a particular warm-up and a weather app checked with unreasonable frequency.</p>
        <h2>We know the pattern.</h2>
        <p>Weekends become draw sheets. Friends become opponents. The final set develops sequels. A racquet appears in photographs where a racquet has no practical reason to be.</p>
        <p>Racquet Habit exists for the space between sport and daily life—for people who do not need encouragement to play, only better things to carry with them.</p>
        <blockquote>One more set is not a plan. It is a recurring condition.</blockquote>
        <h2>The uniform is deliberately composed.</h2>
        <p>No loud performance slogans. No borrowed club crest. No claim that every point is a metaphor for greatness. We prefer useful materials, exact typography and visual devices built from the game itself.</p>
        <p>The outside is restrained because the behavior is expressive enough: stringing with precision, repeating service motions, replaying the same point at lunch, remaining in damp socks much longer than good judgment recommends.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="article-interlude">
      <EditorialImage
        src="/images/editorial/habit-field-study.webp"
        alt="An illustrated field study of a repeat tennis player"
        caption="Habit field study"
        plate="Figure 03"
        ratio="portrait"
      />
      <div>
        <span class="site-kicker">Three working rules</span>
        <ol>
          <li><b>01</b><span>Play often.</span><p>Court hours are never quite over.</p></li>
          <li><b>02</b><span>Choose precisely.</span><p>Fewer pieces, better considered, used until they acquire a record.</p></li>
          <li><b>03</b><span>Leave room for another.</span><p>The last set is almost always a myth.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="annual-article__closing">
      <p>The habit does not need curing. It needs a clean shirt, something cold and a table held for lunch.</p>
      <a class="paper-button" href="/shop">Shop the opening issue <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
